# System information "tasks" (D80) and "printers" (D83), and kinds that are
# not literal text. Task times change from one run to the next, so only
# their shape is shown; names and printers belong to the machine and are
# the same for both Otters on it.
get system information "tasks" into tasks
odd is 0
for each task in tasks
    say name of task
    if lastRunTime of task is not gone
        if length of lastRunTime of task is not 19
            increase odd
        .
    .
    if nextRunTime of task is not gone
        if length of nextRunTime of task is not 19
            increase odd
        .
    .
    if state of task is gone
        increase odd
    .
.
say "tasks with odd times or no state:" odd
get system information "printers" into printers
for each printer in printers
    say printer
.
say "printers is a list"
kind is "TASKS"
get system information kind into again
if length of again is at least 0
    say "tasks again"
.
kind is "print" + "ers"
get system information kind into again
if length of again is length of printers
    say "printers again"
.
kinds are
    "os"
    "Cpu"
.
for each k in kinds
    get system information k into info
    say info
.
try
    kind is 42
    get system information kind into nothing
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
